---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { docs, layers, plannerStages, providers, sourceUrl } from "../../data/site";
---

<SiteLayout title="Architecture — OrbitKV" description="Current KV cache architecture and the planned distributed catalog and router." active="Architecture">
  <div class="container interior">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Architecture</p>
      <h1>Local first.<br /><span class="highlight">Distributed next.</span></h1>
      <p>vLLM and SGLang own GPU pages and execution. OrbitKV owns external cache replicas and transfer leases. Remote-cache recovery comes before KV-aware routing.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="detail-section" aria-labelledby="current-title">
      <h2 id="current-title">What works today</h2>
      <p class="reading-copy">Each inference process connects to a Cache Manager on its own host. UDS and iceoryx2 carry lifecycle and cache commands; CUDA IPC exposes engine-owned GPU pages. The manager stores reusable KV in pinned DRAM and optional SSD. Both adapters passed single-rank DRAM and forced-SSD recovery gates. SGLang defers pending requests through its plugin admission hook; multi-rank serving and concurrent goodput need separate qualification.</p>
      <p class="reading-copy">The multi-node prototype uses a separate, in-memory MetaServer to find candidate replicas. Peer gRPC authorizes transfers; Mooncake moves bytes. Directory restart recovery and high availability are unfinished, so this path remains experimental.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="detail-section" aria-labelledby="crates-title">
      <h2 id="crates-title">Code boundaries</h2>
      <div class="definition-list">
        {layers.map((layer) => (<div><a class="package-name" href={sourceUrl(layer.path)}>{layer.name} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p>{layer.detail}</p></div>))}
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="detail-section" aria-labelledby="compile-title">
      <h2 id="compile-title">Target: a validated state plan</h2>
      <ol class="compile-flow">{plannerStages.map((stage) => (<li><h3>{stage.name}</h3><p>{stage.detail}</p></li>))}</ol>
      <p class="reading-copy">The current hot path uses versioned model and storage identities with native prefix hashes, but still carries raw GPU page IDs. The common state types do not yet prove complete token coverage or a restorable bundle. The proposed planner combines legal recovery boundaries, declared request demand, and measured transfer cost. It remains unimplemented; distributed inventory recovery is also required before routing.</p>
      <dl class="provider-list">{providers.map((provider) => (<div><dt>{provider.name}</dt><dd>{provider.role}</dd></div>))}</dl>
      <p class="reading-copy">The proposed catalog places replicated metadata shards inside Cache Managers and caches candidate locations locally. A small membership service may coordinate epochs; per-block lookups stay off that consensus path. This design is not implemented. A later router may consume the catalog without entering cache transfer.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href={sourceUrl("docs/architecture.md")}>Architecture and safety contract <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </section>
    <section class="detail-section" aria-labelledby="docs-title">
      <h2 id="docs-title">Read the contracts</h2>
      <div class="doc-links">{docs.map((doc) => (<a href={sourceUrl(doc.path)}>{doc.name}<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>))}</div>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
